.TH "GLESHA-STORAGE-CLASS" "1" "" "glesha" "User Commands"
.nh
.ad l
.SH NAME
glesha\-storage\-class \- change the AWS storage class of a snapshot
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBglesha storage\-class\fR SET \-\-class CLASS [options]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Change the storage class of the AWS objects of one snapshot of SET, by default the latest. Objects in a cold class may need to be retrieved first.
.PP
CLASS is one of STANDARD, STANDARD_IA, ONEZONE_IA, INTELLIGENT_TIERING, GLACIER_IR, GLACIER, DEEP_ARCHIVE, or REDUCED_REDUNDANCY.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-class CLASS
New AWS storage class.
.TP
.B \-\-snapshot ID
Snapshot ID, or 'latest' (default: latest).
.TP
.B \-\-storage\-class CLASS
Same as \-\-class.
.SS Remote options
.TP
.B \-\-to REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.TP
.B \-\-from REMOTE...
Limit bucket access to REMOTE.
.PP
REMOTE... takes a comma\-separated list and may be repeated. If \-\-from or \-\-to is given, no other remote is accessed.
.SS Passphrase options
.TP
.B \-\-catalog\-passphrase\-file FILE
Read the catalog passphrase from FILE ('\-': stdin). Without this option, GLESHA_CATALOG_PASSPHRASE or a hidden prompt is used.
.PP
The global options described in glesha(1) are also accepted.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
glesha storage\-class docs \-\-class DEEP_ARCHIVE
glesha storage\-class docs \-\-snapshot ID \-\-class STANDARD
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR glesha (1),
.BR glesha\-move (1),
.BR glesha\-restore (1)
